{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210735,"nonce":"ap3fwo/WgXSpAWHfpRABTWqx90E=","title":"CallKnownFunc slow paths truncated args at 3","message":"Fixed; see git log for the landing commit. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n**Resolved 2026-05-29 — root cause + fix below.**\n\n\n`Instruction::CallKnownFunc` in `src/codegen/cranelift_backend.rs` had\nthree call-emission paths, two of which silently truncated arity:\n\n1. Cached-class fast path (line ~4757): gated on `args.len() \u003c= 4`\n   but emitted `wren_known_call_3_nocheck` for ANY arity \u003e= 3, with\n   `args.iter().take(3)` dropping arg 4. So a 4-arg call lost its\n   last user arg.\n2. No-cached-class fallback (line ~4830): same shape — emitted\n   `wren_known_call_3` and silently dropped args 4..N. So 5+ arg\n   methods called from the JIT had every arg past index 2 read as\n   garbage (whatever was in the inbound register slot).\n\nThe `wren_known_call_N` family in `src/codegen/runtime_fns.rs` only\ncovers N = 0..=3 (both regular and `_nocheck` variants), so any path\nthat used those helpers to dispatch a \u003e3-arg method was structurally\nunsound.\n\nHot example: Renderer2D's `pushVertex_(head, px, py, u, v, r, g, b, a)`\n— 9 user args. The first 3 (`head, px, py`) came through; `u, v, r,\ng, b, a` arrived as null bits (TAG_NULL = 0x7FFC...), surfacing as\n`Float32Array[head + k] = px` writes with k ∈ {4,5,6,7} (the four\nvertex components per quad corner: r, g, b, a).\n\n\n`src/codegen/cranelift_backend.rs` `CallKnownFunc`:\n\n- Cached-class fast path gate tightened to `args.len() \u003c= 3` so the\n  `_nocheck` helper's arity matches the call site exactly; arity 4+\n  falls through to the new generic dispatch tail.\n- No-cached-class tail rewritten: arity 0..=3 keeps the\n  `wren_known_call_N` direct call (preserves the devirtualization\n  hint); arity 4+ routes through `emit_wren_call`, which picks\n  `wren_call_N` for 4..=8 and `wren_call_dynamic` for 9+.\n- CHA path's inner helper block (lines ~4194-4220) cleaned of stale\n  `.min(3)` / `.take(3)` (gate was already `args.len() \u003c= 3` so the\n  truncation was harmless but misleading).\n\n`src/runtime/core/typed_array.rs` `Float32Array[_]=` debug print\nremoved; error message restored to its terse form.\n\n`hatch/examples/game/fruit-slicer/main.wren` module-header\nworkaround note removed.\n\n\n- fruit-slicer ran 6 s in `--mode tiered` cleanly: splash → loading\n  → ready → playing transitions, no `Float32Array[_]=: value must\n  be a number` errors.\n- `cargo test --release --features cranelift --lib` — 914/914 pass.\n- `cargo test --release --features cranelift --test e2e` — 114/114\n  pass (the 2 failures on first run were pre-existing parallel-exec\n  flakes in `e2e_jit_nbody` / `e2e_tiered_backedge_enters_osr_entry_in_method`;\n  re-run clean).\n- `cargo test --release --features cranelift,aot --test aot_runtime`\n  — 21/21 pass.\n- `hatch test packages/hatch-game` — 102/102; `hatch-gpu` — 46/46;\n  `hatch-hud` — 20/20.\n\n\n- `emit_wren_call` helper (added earlier this session, lines 192-249\n  in `cranelift_backend.rs`) — the consolidated dispatcher that\n  picks `wren_call_N` for 0..=8 and `wren_call_dynamic` for 9+.\n  Every `CallKnownFunc` slow path now routes through this; without\n  the tightened gate above, the fast paths still truncated.\n- `call_jit_fn` / `call_jit_cached` extended to arities 0..=16 in\n  `src/runtime/vm_interp.rs` and `src/codegen/runtime_fns.rs` — these\n  are the interpreter→JIT bridge dispatchers; they wouldn't have been\n  hit by this specific bug (Renderer2D batches inside one JIT'd\n  function) but they had the same arity-truncation shape and are now\n  also sound.\n\n\n- Any `match args.len() { _ =\u003e \"wren_*_N\" }` with N below the call\n  site's actual maximum arity is a silent truncation. Either the\n  arity table needs to grow OR the path needs an explicit dynamic\n  fallback. The compiler can't help here because the helper's\n  signature is opaque to it.\n- The symptom of arity-truncation bugs in this codebase is\n  `null`-valued args inside callee bodies, NOT a panic at dispatch\n  time — the JIT'd function reads whatever was in the inbound\n  register, which on aarch64 is whatever the caller left in x4..x7.\n  If the caller cleared those registers (or never touched them),\n  the callee reads `0` which decodes as `null` in the NaN-box.","files":null}]}